Freebuff is not a search engine and not a chat box that only writes text. It is a loop: it reads your project, decides on one action, uses a tool, reads the result, and decides again — until the job is done or it needs something from you.

Four words are easy to mix up:
* '''Model''' — writes the answer and picks the next action.
* '''Agent''' — gives the model a role, instructions, your project and a set of tools.
* '''Tool''' — does one concrete thing: read a file, search text, run a command.
* '''Runtime''' — where that happens: your computer or a cloud workspace.

The project is public: [https://github.com/CodebuffAI/freebuff github.com/CodebuffAI/freebuff], licence Apache-2.0. It is often described as the free alternative to Claude Code, Codex CLI, Cursor, Windsurf and Devin.

== Who is Buffy? ==
'''Buffy''' is the name of the AI agent you talk to — "ask Buffy" means the AI in the chat window. The name is also the app's mascot and appears on the [https://freebuff.com/store/buffy-on-fire-t-shirt "Buffy on Fire" T-shirt] in the official store.

Inside Freebuff the main loop is called '''base3''': one agent investigates, edits and checks with its own tools. Helper agents sit on top of it — a research assistant, and in some setups code subagents. In Codebuff's documentation, "Buffy" is the orchestrator agent, which is where the name comes from.

