The model list and the exact plan bonuses are on the [[Details|Details page]].

== What are its limits? ==
* Vague requests give vague results — say what "done" looks like.
* It will not type your passwords or log in for you.
* No OS sandbox on Desktop: commands run with your own user rights.
* It cannot promise perfect code; a green build is evidence about the build, not about everything.
* A Cloud chat works on a copy of the project; merging is yours, through git.

== How do I start? ==
# Open [https://freebuff.com freebuff.com] and download the desktop app, or open the web app.
# Or use the terminal: <code>npm install -g freebuff</code>, then <code>freebuff</code>.
# Open a project folder, or start an empty one.
# Ask something small first: ''"Explain what this project does."''
# Read the answer, then give the next small step.

Brief it like a ticket: '''what''' to do, '''where''' it may touch, and '''how''' you will know it worked.

* Start in '''Plan''' mode on an unfamiliar project: nothing can change while you look around.
* One small step at a time beats "build the whole app".
* Keep the project in git so a bad change can be undone.

== Common questions ==
; Do I need to know programming?
: No, but it helps. Say clearly what you want and check the result.

; Is it really free?
: Yes — ads pay for the models, and no card or API key is required. Paid plans exist for more model time.

; Can it break my project?
: It can make mistakes. Use Plan mode first for big changes, and keep the project in git.

; Where does my code go?
: On Desktop it stays in the folder you opened. On Cloud it runs in a cloud workspace for that project.

Longer answers, the model list and the glossary are on the [[Details|Details page]].

